// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
; specs/t27f/reel_gf16_nmse.t27 -- the second real T27F reel, and the first in another domain:
; research, "how close does GF16 come to bfloat16", as the project's own NMSE protocol asks it.
; gHashTag/trinity#1677 wants at least two very different domains on one widget and one workflow,
; and a 27-step map that is source-grounded with its gaps named. The first reel
; (reel_t27_basics.t27) is a course, routed to engineering; this one is a benchmark, routed to
; research, and both go through the same code: topic_engine.t27 decides, topic_reel.t27 checks,
; reel.t27 and deck.t27 draw. Nothing below is a rule of this file's own.

; SOURCE: gHashTag/t27 at SOURCE_COMMIT, measured on MEASURED_ON. The protocol spec
; specs/benchmarks/gf16_bfloat16_nmse.t27 and its mirror docs/GF16_BFLOAT16_NMSE_PROTOCOL.md, the
; manifest schema schemas/nmse-protocol-v1.json, the roadmap docs/SCIENTIFIC_IMPROVEMENT_PLAN.md
; (PUB-01, PUB-02), the PUB-02 run harness specs/benchmarks/gf16_bfloat16_nmse_run.t27 and the
; manifest it wrote, RUN_MANIFEST (#10021), and what the repo already holds about GF16. Every cell
; names its source in SOURCES; a cell with none is a gap and says in MISSING what would ground it.

; BRIEF is the first three sentences of the protocol spec's header, verbatim. route_brief
; counts gf16 twice and benchmark once, no other list is hit, so the domain is DOMAIN_RESEARCH.

; LENSES: one row per lens. Steps 1-9 are the formats and why they compare at all; 10-18 the protocol
; and the one run it asks for; 19-27 what may be said and what the repo has said so far.

; MEASURED on 2026-10-18:
;   - grounded: the source is in the repo at SOURCE_COMMIT (path and section in SOURCES).
;   - test: t27c test-report and t27b test --check on the Railway lab passed all 7 tests of the
;     protocol spec; a planted GF16_MANT_BITS = 8 turned 2 of them red under both, so they are real.
;     The harness's own tests check its procedure, not the committed manifest, so no step of the
;     run (16, 17, 25) is marked as tested; on a DELIVER step a test would not count anyway.
;   - review: the PRs that wrote the protocol (#1399), the spec rewrite (#5947) and the run (#10021)
;     have 0 reviews.
;   - live: GET https://t27.ai/t27/files/<path> returned 200 for the protocol spec and the schema,
;     and 404 for the doc, FORMAT-SPEC-001.json, gf16_bench_results.json, the crosswalk, the paper
;     draft, the harness and the manifest; a made-up path returned 404, so 200 is not a catch-all.
; The engine asks a research LEARN step for a source link, a PRACTICE step for a review or a passing
; test, and a DELIVER step for a review. So: 15 published (sourced, earned, and live), 1 verified
; (reporting rules: sourced, not live), 9 drafts (practice or deliver steps with neither a test nor a
; review, three of them the run's own cells) and 2 gaps.

; THE RUN. PUB-02 asks for one sealed bench/results/nmse-*.json. Until #10021 the repo held none, and
; steps 16, 17 and 25 (the run, its schema check, the ratio per distribution) were gaps. They now cite
; RUN_HARNESS and RUN_MANIFEST, and they are DRAFTS, not verified: each is a DELIVER step, a research
; DELIVER step is verified by a review, and the run has none. The manifest is a software run on the
; Railway lab (runner.host_arch x86_64), not a silicon measurement.
; THE GAPS that remain: the chip repo's manifest, gHashTag/tt-trinity-gamma
; tests/vectors/nmse_gf16_bf16.golden.json at GAMMA_COMMIT, pins the seeds but says measured_silicon
; false and harness_committed false; and the paper draft has no Delta_dB yet (PUB-02 allowed one only
; after the manifest, and attaching the manifest to the draft is still open). The older GF16/BF16
; numbers, conformance/gf16_bench_results.json (2026-04-05, no seed, no seal), are drawn as a draft
; that the protocol itself says does not count.

; Not claimed: this reel quotes no NMSE value, no ratio and no winner; the manifest holds the numbers
; and is the only place to read them. Nothing here is silicon. No GIF or MP4; stills only, for the chat.
; phi^2 + 1/phi^2 = 3 | TRINITY

